{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"50d61844-03e1-47e6-9599-4d79a818d07e","agentId":"ad654ba1b8630e5fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are modifying a CadQuery machine model (AUTOKITCH food line, HAT v3 → v3.4). Work ONLY in this build tree:\nB = C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad\\b3\\arastirma\\_uretec\nPython files live in B\\h3\\ (run scripts from B as cwd, e.g. `python -u h3/xxx.py`; some use `python ob_calistir.py h3/xxx.py` — read each file's docstring \"Çalıştır\" line). World coords in mm: x along the line, y up (floor 0), z depth (front +79, back −830).\n\nGOAL (owner's instruction, Turkish: \"harç borusu düz insin, ona göre sola taşı\"): In the TOPPING module the upper-floor harç (lahmacun paste) Beldos UNO doser currently sits at x 2247 while its spreader (yayıcı) below is at x 2160, so the Ø42 product hose jogs 87 mm left at y 1290 (see HORTUM[\"harc\"] and X_UST in h3/h3_topping_v1.py). Move the WHOLE upper-floor harç unit 87 mm LEFT so its axis is x = 2160 (= X_YAYICI[\"harc\"]) and the hose drops with NO x-jog (it may keep z offsets like the sos hose: forward to z −90, down, back to −170, down to the TC inlet at y 1216). Everything belonging to that unit moves with it: UNO body + motor/gearbox, hopper `harc_hazne_bizim` (380 wide → becomes 1970–2350), pneumatic cylinder `harc__pnomatik_*`, `harc_silindir_konsolu`, `harc_mil_gecis_kovani` and the shaft hole through the cold-box back wall, the shelf (raf) hose hole + seal, pneumatic hoses from the valve island to that cylinder, any brackets. Do NOT move the spreader, the sos unit, the lower floor, the tabla mechanism.\n\nKNOWN CONFLICT you must solve: after the move the harç cylinder/konsol/shaft occupy about x 2134–2186, y 1534–1633, z −827…−561 (shaft kovan z −635…−565 passes through the back wall). That lands inside the evaporator cassette `evap_kaseti_*` (x 1676–2216, y 1350–1765, z −826…−630, in the dry compartment \"kuru bölme\" behind the cold box) and its back-wall window parts `arka_duvar_kaset_yuzu`, `kaset_penceresi_dolgusu` (x 1698–2194, y 1405–1743, z −630…−570). Required solution: make the cassette L-shaped by notching its TOP-RIGHT corner (all shell layers: dış sac, PU, iç sac, ısı kesici çerçeve, ara sacı, fan plakası, askı if needed) so the moved harç cylinder, konsol, shaft and kovan clear by ≥ 5 mm; also cut the shaft passage (with clearance) through the window filler/back face. Keep UNCHANGED: `evap_kaseti_lamel_paketi` (x 1719–2116, y 1443–1580), the two Sanyo fans, `arka_hava_kanali_alt/ust` (x 1726–2106), refrigerant lines, drain. If the collector/TXV envelope `evap_kaseti_kollektor_TXV_zarfi` (x 2117–2166, y 1450–1550) intersects the notch, shorten/lower it within the cassette keeping it at the coil's right end. Insulation must stay continuous (stepped PU wall, no gaps). Also check the upper floor of the cold box: moved hopper/UNO must not collide with the sos unit, the shelf, the back-wall supply grille, front lids, or anything else. Keep all existing x-station constraints in the file comments valid.\n\nAlso update the comments/docstring in h3_topping_v1.py (X_UST harç 2160, hose straight, cassette notch, date 1 Eki 2026) and keep the module's contract (same function names, same part naming style; new parts get Turkish snake_case names). Edit files IN PLACE (h3_topping_v1.py, and h3_hesap_v1.py / h3_tu_v1.py / h3_tc_v1.py only if truly needed). Do NOT touch any h3_elk_*.py, h3_elektrik_v1.py, hat3_montaj_*.py, yap_*.py files, and do NOT run hat3_montaj_*.py or h3_elektrik_v1.py (another agent runs those).\n\nVERIFY: run the TOPPING's own checks that exist in B\\h3 (h3_topping_denetim_v1.py — static clash; h3_topping_supurme_v1.py — sweep), plus any self-check in h3_topping_v1.py, and additionally write a small script that builds the TOPPING parts and does a real solid intersection check between every moved/modified part and all other TOPPING parts (report any overlap > 0.5 mm³). Compare against the baseline (run the checks once BEFORE editing to know pre-existing known overlaps, so you only report new ones). These CAD scripts can take minutes; use long timeouts.\n\nRETURN: a concise report (Turkish is fine): what moved and by how much, the exact notch box removed from the cassette, any other geometry changed, the check results before/after (counts), and anything you could not solve. Don't paste large file contents."},"uuid":"a396af2d-fec8-4b24-936c-de64b3cb0bd1","timestamp":"2026-10-01T12:49:57.385Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
